silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_02_typed_legs_and_atlas_sections_04_diagram_inventory_table_concrete_anchor_6#measurementsystemsengineer_reader silm:hasLongDescription "The MeasurementSystemsEngineer_reader is the cross-domain reader: a measurement-systems engineer who reads the twisted-arrow as the formal quality/procedure non-identity. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'MeasurementSystemsEngineer_reader', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
